{
 "manifestVersion": "traceweave-m22-fixture-manifest-draft-1",
 "note": "Frozen M2.2 fixture manifest. Each UC-1 example-matrix row has at least one positive case derived by hand (derivation 'hand'). Spans are half-open UTF-8 byte offsets [start, end). Positive cases list their REPORTABLE regions only (regionsListed 'reportable'); companion cases list every region ('all'). Other regions are covered by the body digest. An implementation passes M2.2 only if, for every case, its catalogues and body reproduce these digests and every listed span (N/N).",
 "derivationRule": "A vector is hand-derived when both of these hold: (a) Judgments are written by a person. Every judgment the contract leaves to a reader is written by a person from the contract text. That covers the token boundaries, classes and texts; inserted tokens; the outcome status; and the error code and the position of the defect. For matching vectors it also covers which regions match, and the outcome. (b) Arithmetic is computed and rechecked. Everything that is pure arithmetic over those judgments is computed by the specification's own checker or builder, which is not an implementation under test. That covers byte spans located from the hand-written token texts, SHA-256 hashes, window selection, fingerprints, digests and canonical bytes. At least one independent recomputation, by a clean-room reviewer or a second checker, confirms it. A vector whose lexical layer was first produced by a tool and then reviewed is not hand-derived, and must be labelled otherwise. Applied to this manifest: which vectors serve as positive and companion cases of each UC-1 example-matrix row is written by hand; each case's derivation label is the matching vector's own (matching.json derivationRule). The listed digests, outcomes and spans are copied by build_gates.py from the bodies build_vectors.py computed, and check_gates.py recomputes every body and requires every digest and span to match.",
 "matchingVectorsFile": "matching.json",
